  - q: "Will WhatsApp ban my number?"
    a: "Not from this. Sending WhatsApp messages automatically to people who haven't written to you first breaks WhatsApp's business rules, so it never does that. It prepares each message, and you send it from your phone in one tap, starting with a few dozen new chats a day."
  - q: "Do I have to write the messages?"
    a: "No. The research and the first draft are done for you. You read, edit if you like, and approve, usually in batches, in a few minutes a day."
  - q: "Does it use AI?"
    a: "Yes, to research businesses and draft messages. A person approves every message, and nothing it reads on the web can make it do anything."
  - q: "What do you need from me?"
    a: "A mailbox to send from, your WhatsApp Business number, and an idea of who you want to reach. We'll help you sharpen the last one."
  - q: "What does it cost?"
    a: "A fixed quote to set it up for your business, after a free conversation. Running costs depend on how many businesses you want to reach, and we show you those numbers before you start."
  - q: "Do you use it yourselves?"
    a: "Yes. Nirmaan finds its own clients with it. That's why it exists."
---
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
        <h2 class="section__title display" id="problem-title">Finding customers is the&nbsp;hard part.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__text">Most small businesses look for new customers in one of three ways. Each works, up to a point.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="mk-problems" role="list">
      {%- for p in problems %}
      <li class="mk-problem" data-reveal style="--d: {{ loop.index0 }}">
        <p class="mono mk-problem__n">0{{ loop.index }}</p>
        <h3 class="mk-problem__title">{{ p.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ p.text }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="mk-answer display" data-reveal>Nirmaan Marketing does the research and the first draft. <span class="accent">You keep the&nbsp;judgement.</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">See it work</p>
        <h2 class="section__title display" id="demo-title">One campaign, start to&nbsp;finish.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__text">Seven steps, from a goal in plain words to a reply in your inbox. Press any step, or let it play.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tour" data-tour>
      <div class="tour__bar">
        <div class="tour__steps" role="tablist" aria-label="Campaign steps">
          {%- set steps = ["Goal", "Find", "Check", "Draft", "Approve", "Listen", "Learn"] %}
          {%- for s in steps %}
          <button class="tour__step" type="button" role="tab" id="tour-tab-{{ loop.index }}" aria-controls="tour-beat-{{ loop.index }}" aria-selected="{{ 'true' if loop.first else 'false' }}" tabindex="{{ '0' if loop.first else '-1' }}"><span class="mono">0{{ loop.index }}</span> {{ s }}</button>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
        <button class="tour__replay mono" type="button" data-tour-replay>Replay</button>
      </div>
      <div class="tour__progress" aria-hidden="true"><span data-tour-progress></span></div>

      <div class="tour__stage">
        {#- 1. Goal -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" role="tabpanel" id="tour-beat-1" aria-labelledby="tour-tab-1">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title"><span class="mono">01</span> Write the goal in plain words.</h3>
            <p>It turns the goal into a plan you can check and edit: what to search for, where, and what the first messages lead with.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b class="mono">New campaign</b></div>
            <div class="console__body">
              <p class="console__label mono" data-i style="--i: 0">Goal</p>
              <p class="console__input" data-i style="--i: 1">Dental and skin clinics in Ahmedabad and Surat that still book appointments by phone.</p>
              <p class="console__label mono" data-i style="--i: 2">Plan</p>
              <ul class="console__rows" role="list">
                <li data-i style="--i: 3"><span>dental clinic</span><span class="mono">Ahmedabad</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 4"><span>dental clinic</span><span class="mono">Surat</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 5"><span>skin clinic</span><span class="mono">Ahmedabad</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 6"><span>skin clinic</span><span class="mono">Surat</span></li>
              </ul>
              <p class="console__note" data-i style="--i: 7">First messages lead with: <b>booking online, day and night</b></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {#- 2. Find -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" role="tabpanel" id="tour-beat-2" aria-labelledby="tour-tab-2">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title"><span class="mono">02</span> It finds businesses that fit.</h3>
            <p>Maps and the web, one search at a time, every day. Each business appears once, with where it was found.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b class="mono">Found today</b></div>
            <div class="console__body">
              <ul class="console__rows console__rows--found" role="list">
                <li data-i style="--i: 0"><span>Riverside Dental Studio</span><span class="mono">Ahmedabad · maps</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 1"><span>Lotus Skin Clinic</span><span class="mono">Surat · maps</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 2"><span>Northgate Dental Care</span><span class="mono">Ahmedabad · web</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 3"><span>Banyan Skin &amp; Hair</span><span class="mono">Surat · maps</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 4"><span>Meridian Smiles</span><span class="mono">Ahmedabad · maps</span></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {#- 3. Check -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" role="tabpanel" id="tour-beat-3" aria-labelledby="tour-tab-3">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title"><span class="mono">03</span> It looks for a real reason to write.</h3>
            <p>It reads the business's own website. If there's nothing true and specific to say, it doesn't write.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b class="mono">riverside-dental.example</b></div>
            <div class="console__body">
              <p class="console__label mono" data-i style="--i: 0">What the site shows</p>
              <ul class="console__signals" role="list">
                <li class="is-yes" data-i style="--i: 1">Appointments by phone call only</li>
                <li class="is-yes" data-i style="--i: 2">No way to book after hours</li>
                <li class="is-yes" data-i style="--i: 3">Pages hard to use on a phone</li>
                <li class="is-no" data-i style="--i: 4">Online payments: not needed</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="console__verdict" data-i style="--i: 5"><b>Good fit.</b> Worth a message about booking online.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {#- 4. Draft -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" role="tabpanel" id="tour-beat-4" aria-labelledby="tour-tab-4">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title"><span class="mono">04</span> It drafts a message in your voice.</h3>
            <p>Short, first person, one true observation and one small next step. Every message ends with a way to opt out.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b class="mono">Draft · email</b></div>
            <div class="console__body console__mail">
              <p class="mono console__meta" data-i style="--i: 0">To: hello@riverside-dental.example</p>
              <p class="console__subject" data-i style="--i: 1">Evening appointments at Riverside</p>
              <p data-i style="--i: 2">Hello Dr. Mehta,</p>
              <p data-i style="--i: 3"><mark>I noticed appointments at Riverside can only be booked by phone, so patients who call after hours can't get through.</mark> A simple booking page could take those bookings while you're closed.</p>
              <p data-i style="--i: 4">Would a 15-minute call this week be useful?</p>
              <p data-i style="--i: 5">Sahaj</p>
              <p class="console__optout" data-i style="--i: 6">Not relevant? Reply “stop” and we won’t contact you again.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {#- 5. Approve -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" role="tabpanel" id="tour-beat-5" aria-labelledby="tour-tab-5">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title"><span class="mono">05</span> You approve. Then it sends like a person.</h3>
            <p>Email goes from your mailbox in working hours, one at a time. WhatsApp is ready for you to send from your phone in one tap.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b class="mono">Waiting for you</b></div>
            <div class="console__body">
              <ul class="console__rows console__rows--queue" role="list">
                <li data-i style="--i: 0"><span>Riverside Dental Studio</span><span class="console__chip is-done mono">Approved</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 1"><span class="console__sub">Email · sends at 11:42, working hours</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 2"><span>Lotus Skin Clinic</span><span class="console__chip mono">Send on WhatsApp</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 3"><span class="console__sub">One tap from your phone</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 4"><span>Meridian Smiles</span><span class="console__chip mono">Read and approve</span></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {#- 6. Listen -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" role="tabpanel" id="tour-beat-6" aria-labelledby="tour-tab-6">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title"><span class="mono">06</span> It listens to replies.</h3>
            <p>A reply stops the follow-ups and becomes a lead. Anyone who says stop is never contacted again.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b class="mono">Inbox</b></div>
            <div class="console__body">
              <div class="console__reply" data-i style="--i: 0">
                <p class="mono console__meta">Riverside Dental Studio · Re: Evening appointments</p>
                <p>“Yes, call me on Thursday after 6.”</p>
              </div>
              <ul class="console__events" role="list">
                <li data-i style="--i: 1">Follow-up cancelled</li>
                <li class="is-blue" data-i style="--i: 2">New lead created</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="console__reply" data-i style="--i: 3">
                <p class="mono console__meta">Northgate Dental Care · Re: Online bookings</p>
                <p>“stop”</p>
              </div>
              <ul class="console__events" role="list">
                <li data-i style="--i: 4">Added to do-not-contact, for good</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {#- 7. Learn -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" role="tabpanel" id="tour-beat-7" aria-labelledby="tour-tab-7">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title"><span class="mono">07</span> Every week, it learns what works.</h3>
            <p>Replies by segment, city and channel. It moves effort toward what gets answers, and tells you what it changed.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b class="mono">Weekly review</b></div>
            <div class="console__body">
              <p class="console__label mono" data-i style="--i: 0">Replies by segment</p>
              <ul class="console__bars" role="list">
                <li data-i style="--i: 1"><span>Dental clinics</span><i style="--w: 0.9"></i></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 2"><span>Skin clinics</span><i style="--w: 0.5"></i></li>
              </ul>
              <p class="console__label mono" data-i style="--i: 3">Next week</p>
              <ul class="console__events" role="list">
                <li class="is-blue" data-i style="--i: 4">More dental clinics</li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 5">Surat searched first</li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 6">A little more email, a little less WhatsApp</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="tour__note mono">Illustration with sample businesses. Not real data.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What it does</p>
        <h2 class="section__title display" id="features-title">The research and the writing, done for&nbsp;you.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__text">Everything that makes personal outreach slow, handled, with the decisions left to you.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="mk-features" role="list">
      {%- for f in features %}
      <li class="mk-feature" data-reveal style="--d: {{ loop.index0 % 3 }}">
        {% glyph f.glyph, "mk-feature__glyph" %}
        <h3 class="mk-feature__title">{{ f.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ f.text }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="outcomes-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">How it markets you</p>
      <h2 class="section__title display" id="outcomes-title">More of the right conversations.</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="mk-outcomes" role="list">
      {%- for o in outcomes %}
      <li class="mk-outcome" data-reveal style="--d: {{ loop.index0 }}">
        <p class="mono mk-outcome__n">0{{ loop.index }}</p>
        <h3 class="mk-outcome__title">{{ o.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ o.text }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="guards-title">
  <div class="wrap mk-split">
    <div data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Built in, not optional</p>
      <h2 class="section__title display" id="guards-title">Outreach that protects your&nbsp;name.</h2>
      <p class="section__text">These rules are part of the system. They can't be switched off by accident.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="mk-guards" role="list" data-reveal>
      {%- for g in guards %}
      <li>{{ g }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="who-title">
  <div class="wrap mk-split">
    <div data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Who it's for</p>
      <h2 class="section__title display" id="who-title">Businesses that win work by&nbsp;talking.</h2>
      <p class="section__text">If a good customer is worth a conversation, it's worth finding them. It isn't for promotional blasts to the public.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="mk-audience" role="list" data-reveal>
      {%- for a in audience %}
      <li>{{ a }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="setup-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Getting started</p>
        <h2 class="section__title display" id="setup-title">Set up with you, in four&nbsp;steps.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__text">We set it up around your customer and your voice, run the first campaign with you, and look after it from then on.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="mk-setup" role="list">
      {%- for s in setup %}
      <li class="mk-step" data-reveal style="--d: {{ loop.index0 }}">
        <p class="mono mk-step__n">Step {{ loop.index }}</p>
        <h3 class="mk-step__title">{{ s.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ s.text }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="mk-faq-title">
  <div class="wrap faq-layout">
    <div data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
      <h2 class="section__title display" id="mk-faq-title">What people ask&nbsp;first.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq" data-reveal>
      {%- for item in faq %}
      <details{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}>
        <summary>{{ item.q }}<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <p class="faq__answer">{{ item.a }}</p>
      </details>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
